---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { loadAll } from "../lib/data.server";

const { meals, recipes } = loadAll();
---

<SiteLayout title="Plan — Cookbook" description="Build a weekly meal plan from meals and recipes.">
  <section style="padding-block: 44px 0;">
    <p class="lbl">Not built yet</p>
    <h1 style="margin-top: 10px;">Plan</h1>
    <p style="max-width: 58ch; margin: 16px 0 0; font-size: 1.08rem; color: var(--ink-2);">
      This is where meals and standalone recipes get dropped onto days and slots to build a week.
      The plan then generates both outputs: a cooking sheet and a shopping list.
    </p>
    <p style="max-width: 58ch; margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--muted);">
      The engine underneath is already done and tested — plan expansion, servings scaling, unit
      merging, pantry subtraction and aisle grouping all work. What is missing is the drag-and-drop
      board on top of it.
    </p>
    <div style="display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 26px;">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/meals">Browse {meals.length} meal{meals.length === 1 ? "" : "s"}</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/recipes">Browse {recipes.length} recipes</a>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top: 30px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted);">
      In the meantime, any meal page shows its combined ingredients merged across every recipe in it.
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
